WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:07.470
It’s the second most populated country
on Earth, has the seventh biggest economy,

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:15.090
has one of the 10 biggest military budgets
in the world, and is a nuclear power.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:19.499
However, India is a stranger in political
terms.

00:00:19.499 --> 00:00:23.949
If I asked you who was the Prime Minister
of India, could you tell me?

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:31.470
Now, I am aware that many of you will know,
especially if you are viewing this from India...

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:44.690
But, if you don’t, don’t worry, that happens
a lot.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.851
On the 26th May 2014, after an absolute majority
which had not been seen in 30 years, Narendra

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:52.640
Modi became India´s Prime Minister.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.640
Modi´s Mission?

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.040
It was clear: boost growth, investment, and
create millions of jobs.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:05.570
In conclusion, turn India in a superpower
capable of competing with China on an economic,

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:10.719
military and political level.

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:15.109
Now India is, dear VisualPolitik viewers,
something of an eternal promise.

00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:20.869
It’s always the country which seems to be
the next to take off... but never really seems

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:21.869
to take off.

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:35.610
We can see that with a quick look at India
and China’s GDP and its development in the

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.229
last decades...

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:41.479
So, with Modi´s victory, expectations were
high again, and India once again has become

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:42.479
the talk of the town.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:47.789
Modi himself repeats over and over again that
the 21st Century will be India´s century.

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:52.579
But let’s first take a quick look at Modi
himself.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.539
-WHO IS NARENDRA MODI?-

00:01:55.539 --> 00:02:01.830
Vegetarian, single, and a Yoga enthusiast:
Modi escapes the traditional politician profile.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:06.499
He comes from a family of limited means and
he used to help his father sell tea in a train

00:02:06.499 --> 00:02:07.499
station when he was a child.

00:02:07.499 --> 00:02:11.360
This has helped him to earn the sympathy of
many poor people in the country, who see him

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:21.030
as an example that “rags to riches” in
India does sometimes work.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:26.150
His political ideology has always been very
attached to Hinduism, but not always with

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.150
a moderate approach.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:34.099
In fact, before getting involved with the
BJP party, he was part of &nbsp;RSS, an extreme

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:39.120
right-wing political party who had Nathuram
Godse as a member, Mahatma Gandhi's assassin.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:46.120
For 13 years, between 2001 and 2014, Modi
was the regional Prime Minister in the State

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.120
of Gujarat.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:53.459
Gujarat, with its 65 million inhabitants,
has become, under Modi´s leadership, India´s

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:59.870
economic driver with an average annual growth
of more than 10%.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.430
Alongside these impressive figures, social
welfare has also improved.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:08.849
Almost every home has access to plumbing,
electricity, and pre-school education.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.730
While the General election was taking place,
Modi promised to replicate Gujarat´s success

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.379
through the rest of India.

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:21.900
Furthermore, he promised to do it in 10 years
- just two political terms.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:38.540
That is because, for Modi, 2022 is key: the
75th anniversary on India’s independence.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:44.920
The country will also surpass China as the
most populated, with more than 1600 million

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:55.079
people and, according to Modi, it will become
clear that this is India’s Century.

00:03:55.079 --> 00:04:07.700
But it will not be easy: India is a country
whose population is growing by 28 inhabitants

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.730
every minute.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:14.579
-INDIA’S BIG TROUBLES-

00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:20.000
India has several problems, but three stand
out as particularly important:

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.370
1 - India is bureaucrat's paradise.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:28.810
In fact, if that were to be the key to prosperity,
India would probably be the wealthiest country

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.040
in the world.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.810
Unfortunately, bureaucracy, instead of encouraging
business, prevents it.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:39.580
(John Kerry’s statement saying India’s
bureaucracy could compromise the economical

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.440
success of the country).

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.250
According to the Doing Business Report of
the World Bank, which estimates how easy it

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.139
is to do business, India occupies the 130th
position.

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:56.270
Each step on the way to opening a business
requires tons of documents, and the taxes

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:01.220
are not only high (even though very few pay
them) they are absolute hell to work out.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:05.960
For example, there are not only different
taxes in each state, but sometimes there are

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:12.500
different taxes for each product or for different
models of the same product (as happens with

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.500
vehicles).

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:24.410
It really is a crazy system.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:29.850
Further, absenteeism among public workers
is so high that there have been situations

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:34.000
critical enough to close hospitals because
workers did not show up.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:40.660
2- The regulations in the market as so complex
that it is almost unable to function.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.990
On the borders between states, trucks full
of goods have to stand in endless queues.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:51.470
Not few say it is easier to import that to
buy inside the country.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:56.440
The devastating condition of the country’s
infrastructure does not help either.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:03.349
Further, as a consequence of this, it is estimated
that half the harvest goes to waste before

00:06:03.349 --> 00:06:06.710
even arriving to the country’s markets.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.930
3 – Corruption is quite common in Indian
society.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:15.650
As an example, 50% of all aid provided by
the government to families and the poor end

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.060
up in hands of corrupt politicians and middlemen.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.000
This is the country that Modi has to deal
with.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.639
-THE NEW GOVERNMENT’S POLICIES-

00:06:26.639 --> 00:06:30.810
The revolution some have suggested has not
taken place.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:35.490
However, the truth is the new government has
achieved some advances.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:36.690
We could highlight the following:

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:41.060
- In order to reduce bureaucracy, the government
has created a committee with the purpose of

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:45.310
determining which rules and regulations are
obsolete and need to be eliminated.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:48.020
So far they have done away with more than
1700.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:52.600
- Modi has also eliminated many restrictions
on foreign investment, and has passed the

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:59.100
first bankruptcy law, and has set up a powerful
plan to promote India as a business destination.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:05.250
- They have started an ambitious plan to achieve
better financial inclusion.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.300
This plan has a pretty unpronounceable name
I’m just going to show on the screen.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:14.659
It has already allowed for 200 million people
to have a bank account for the first time.

00:07:14.659 --> 00:07:21.780
This way, government subsidies won’t have
to go through middlemen any more.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:28.169
-The government is considering the implementation
of a flat rate tax on sales at a national

00:07:28.169 --> 00:07:37.979
level to end the chaos of the current tax
system.

00:07:37.979 --> 00:07:41.290
- Modi has further announced an important
investment in infrastructure - $130 billion

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:50.039
will be spent by 2020 on just a railway network

00:07:50.039 --> 00:07:57.100
… But his most risky move was announced
in November 2016.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.939
-INDIA’S CASH CRISIS-

00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:08.750
In order to fight corruption, the government
made 500 and 1000 rupee notes illegal, which

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:13.740
represented more than 85% of all the ‘hard
cash’ in India, a country where almost all

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.100
the payments are made in cash.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:20.900
The goal was to find dirty money and punish
its owners when they went to change it for

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.389
the new design notes.

00:08:23.389 --> 00:08:28.139
However, the plan has been a total disaster:
the government didn’t have enough notes

00:08:28.139 --> 00:08:33.599
to change for the old ones and the countries
ATMs weren't even working properly because

00:08:33.599 --> 00:08:45.470
new notes had different sizes.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.610
This was a botched operation which left the
country moneyless, creating significant damage

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:50.930
to its economy.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.430
Sales fell in November by more than 30%.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.410
Many businesses weren’t able to pay their
workers and many business transactions had

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.410
to be cancelled.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.870
Some studies estimate the damage to be at
least two points of the country's GDP.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.570
That would mean the banknote switch cost India
almost $50 billion.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:08.180
Needless to say it is the poorest citizens
who have suffered the most.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:11.881
The government even tried to justify and disguise
the mess under the premise of it being part

00:09:11.881 --> 00:09:17.370
of a plan to encourage the use of electronic
money...

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:19.430
Ahhh politicians!

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:20.590
-FOREIGN POLICY AGENDA-

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:25.160
Now this is the field where the Prime Minister
has really excelled.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.420
In his first year alone, he visited 19 countries.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:42.300
Despite the fact that he has only been in
power for a short amount of time, he has achieved

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:46.710
some notable advances: the Pakistan treaty
has improved the India/Pakistan relationship,

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:50.820
and a relationship with China has started
dealing with some economic and commercial

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:55.720
issues.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:10:04.880
However, without any doubt, the greatest strength
of Modi’s political agenda has been his

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.760
approach to the US.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:11.010
The chemistry between Obama and Modi has been
quite significant and their encounters have

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.440
been frequent and friendly.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:16.100
They both even published an article together
in the Washington Post.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:21.959
What we need to ask now is: Will Modi reach
his goals?

00:10:21.959 --> 00:10:23.940
They certainly are challenging.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:30.800
It has been made clear to the Prime Minister
how tricky it is to put limits on bureaucracy.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:36.190
Further, Modi has avoided many essential reforms,
such as ending India’s labour regulation,

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:40.790
which is to blame for the fact that 4 out
5 jobs in India are on the grey market.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:46.019
Modi claims to be an admirer of Lee Kuan Yew,
Singapore´s ex-prime minister, but Modi does

00:10:46.019 --> 00:10:51.180
not seem to have the same determination to
transform India’s appalling model.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:55.579
So, that’s our opinion, but what do you
think?

00:10:55.579 --> 00:10:58.370
Do you think the 21st Century will be India’s
century?

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:11.610
If you enjoyed this video please hit that
like button and don’t forget to subscribe,

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:14.490
and, as always, I’ll see you in the next
video!

